# Sokoban — push every crate onto a goal.
#
# A Canvas port of the Seed7 demo `prg/sokoban.sd7` by Thomas Mertes
# (https://seed7.net). The rules, the status panel and the click-to-walk
# control come from there; the 16x16 tile art is this port's own, spelled out
# as pictures further down.
#
# The levels are fifteen of the 155 in Microban, by David W. Skinner
# (originally at users.bentonrea.com/~sasquatch/sokoban/), used on his terms:
# "These sets may be freely distributed provided they remain properly
# credited." `origin` is the number each level carries in that set. Seed7 ships
# the 1982 Thinking Rabbit levels instead, which are a separate copyright and
# not ours to copy.
#
# Seed7 blocks on `getc(KEYBOARD)` inside a per-level `repeat ... until`. A
# Canvas program polls once a frame instead, so that loop is not a state
# machine to rebuild — it disappears. Its locals become fields, its body
# becomes `on_key`, and `tick` runs what is left.
#
# Run it:  culebra examples/games/sokoban.cul        (play)
#          culebra examples/games/sokoban.cul 7      (start on level 7)
#          culebra examples/games/sokoban.cul </dev/null   (plays itself)

ART = 16  # every tile is drawn on a 16x16 grid...
ZOOM = 2  # ...and blitted at ZOOM, so one drawn pixel is a square block
TILE = ART * ZOOM
FONT = ZOOM  # the 8x8 text is scaled to match, so the whole screen is one grid
LINE = 8 * FONT + 4

BOARD_W = 15 * TILE  # the widest and the tallest level, in pixels
BOARD_H = 12 * TILE
PANEL_X = BOARD_W + 16
W = PANEL_X + 20 * 8 * FONT + 16  # the panel holds 20 characters
H = BOARD_H + 3 * FONT * 8        # the board, plus a line to credit the levels

